{"chapter": "conventions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0005", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-remark-big-categories}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60933e2eb73b5869424ecf69d90b96f339f85ff45ff143b7b9fe9b3e0ad8de56", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9f9dcb1584f5b90e190bec36fee9d3559a0728df9a545628259ff2229925797f", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nA category <MATH_0001> consists of a set of objects and, for each pair\nof objects,\na set of morphisms between them. In other words, it is what is called\na ``small'' category in other texts. We will use ``big'' categories\n(categories whose objects form a proper class)\nas well, but only those that are listed in Categories,\nRemark <REF_0001>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:59505035ec4cf3764c083801afc8a84630837a45a1751615667212568a60913a", "unit_id": "tag:0005:paragraph-0001"}
